44
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,160
Gabriel. Solo.

45
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,680
Miku?

46
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:09,320
How dare you refer to me so casually?

47
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:12,520
I only let my closest friends call me Miku,

48
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:15,160
and I don't see a rude klutz like you making that list.

49
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,280
What do you want us to do?

50
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,760
Should we come inside and help with the rescue mission?

51
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,000
No, thank you.

52
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,540
There's so many of you.

53
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:25,320
If you all came, they'd likely hear us from a mile away.

54
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:28,180
Why don't you stay outside and make sure those pesky wizards

55
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:30,260
stay off our tails while we save you-know-who?

56
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,480
Miku, what are you doing here?

57
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,340
Wait a sec.

58
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:40,700
Is this about that promise?

59
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:43,300
Don't go getting the wrong idea, you primate.

60
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:46,200
I wouldn't dream of letting you seal my powers, promise or not.

61
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,780
I didn't come here for you.

62
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:51,240
I came for the sole purpose of adding another spirit to my collection,

63
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:52,860
so don't go thinking we're partners.

64
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,520
Either way, thank you.

65
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,040
I owe you one.

66
00:03:57,860 --> 00:03:59,300
Now die!

67
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:09,300
Oh no, she's completely lost it.

68
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:12,060
You're right!

69
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:19,520
Doesn't look like she's in any state to make decisions right now.

70
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:24,200
It's likely her mind was forced to process too much magical power in too short a time.

71
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:24,640
Mana!

72
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,000
Don't worry.

73
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,300
We're on our way!

74
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:40,240
You dodged.

75
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,580
That wasn't bad at all.

76
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:43,100
I'm actually impressed.

77
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,440
Mana!

78
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:45,440
Mana!

79
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:45,900
Perfect.

80
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:46,900
Two on one.

81
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,280
Be gone!

82
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:49,440
Blast off!

83
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:57,580
Normally, I don't like ganging up two against one,

84
00:04:57,820 --> 00:05:00,360
but if that's the way Ike wants it, then so be it.

85
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:02,840
Mana!

86
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,140
Hey, Mana!

87
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,660
How does it feel now that I've got you cornered?

88
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:07,440
Tell me!

89
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:12,260
Your reflexes are impressive.

90
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:13,440
However...

91
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,760
Did you see that?

92
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:18,580
That's what I call a jackpot!

93
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,260
Sergeant Tomiichi!

94
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,300
You're right on time.

95
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:32,840
Where's Shido?

96
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:34,980
Don't worry about Shido.

97
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:36,080
He's perfectly safe.

98
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,220
He's in building number one right now.

99
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:45,380
You're gonna have to go through me.

100
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:46,880
I'll be happy to.

101
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,700
Well, you're the prettiest one yet.

102
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,760
I'm looking for my friend Toka.

103
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,780
Be a dear and tell me where you're keeping her.

104
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:54,780
Uh, sorry.

105
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,200
That's classified information.

106
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:57,840
If you don't tell, I'll hate you.

107
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:00,080
I'll have no choice but to hate you forever.

108
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:00,900
No!

109
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:01,600
Please!

110
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:02,680
Anything but that!

111
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:05,700
Your friend is quarantined on the 18th floor.

112
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:08,140
If you use this ID, you'll be able to get in.

113
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:09,580
Just don't hate me forever.

114
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:10,820
I would die.

115
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:11,840
Like, seriously.

116
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:12,800
You're sweet.

117
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,640
You see, now that wasn't so terrible, was it?

118
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,600
Like they say, there's more than one way to skin a cat.

119
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:21,060
You're freaking me out.

120
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:23,980
She said the quarantine area was on the 18th floor.

121
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:24,920
Right?

122
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:26,480
Let's go, Miku.

123
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:29,880
Would you please stop acting like we're working together on this mission?

124
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,040
And it grosses me out.

125
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,240
Team, fire at will!

126
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:47,740
Do you think an attack like that is enough to stop someone as powerful as me?

127
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:50,680
I really do hate being underestimated.

128
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,360
What's wrong?

129
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:08,760
Do you know how pathetic you look?

130
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:11,640
If you keep pushing yourself like this, you'll burn out.

131
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:12,940
I told you already.

132
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,960
I'm willing to do whatever it takes to save Toka.

133
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,260
And I don't have time to waste.

134
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:20,420
Oh, yeah, sure.

135
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:22,080
You're a big loser, you know that?

136
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:25,900
Are you that enthralled with the idea of rescuing the tragic heroine?

137
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:30,020
I know you think you're some kind of superhero, Shido, but you're not.

138
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:33,320
Now that you're confronted with the reality of the situation,

139
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:37,320
do you want to take back what you said about Toka being more important than your own life?

140
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:38,740
You can tell the truth.

141
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,300
It won't make me more disappointed in you.

142
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:44,140
When I ask you a question, I expect an answer.

143
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:45,880
Hmm.

144
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:49,280
Ooh, I've got a great idea.

145
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:53,360
Why don't you drop the whole hero act and just give up on saving Toka?

146
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:54,060
It's smart.

147
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:57,540
We could leave this place right now and won't have to worry about dying at the hands of a...

148
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:58,280
Will you shut up?

149
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:05,000
Nobody can ever replace Toka.

150
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:12,600
Please, we both know you can't keep this act up forever.

151
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:16,020
That's all this rescue mission really is in the first place, isn't it?

152
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:16,700
One big show.

153
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:17,800
You've got the wrong idea.

154
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:20,380
Why do you always think the worst of humans?

155
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:22,060
Just shut up!

156
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:25,640
Humans are nothing but toys for my amusement.

157
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:29,360
The men are my slaves, and the girls are my pretty little playthings.

158
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:32,380
That's all humans are worth, and let me tell you, it isn't much.

159
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:34,520
Miku, I don't understand.

160
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:36,100
Why do you hate men so much?

161
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:38,880
And why do you treat people like they're nothing but objects?

162
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:42,040
What happened to you that made you see humans this way?

163
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:45,760
Isn't the answer to your question obvious?

164
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:47,720
It's just the way you people are.

165
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,980
But weren't you a human once?

166
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:57,620
Before phantom or noise or whatever turns you, you were just a girl, a run-of-the-mill human being no different than me, weren't you?

167
00:08:58,380 --> 00:08:59,120
Am I wrong?

168
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:00,380
It's true.

169
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,080
But how did you know that?

170
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:05,440
Let's just say an acquaintance of mine told me.

171
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:07,640
Yod's power is recollection.

172
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:13,500
A powerful technique that gives me a special inside look into some of the target's recent memories.

173
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:19,480
If you're a human being too, Miku, does that mean you hate yourself?

174
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:22,760
It would be much better if you'd shut your mouth, jerk!

175
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,400
What do you know about it anyway?

176
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:26,040
You don't know me at all!

177
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,340
You're right.

178
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:30,200
But maybe if you talk to me, I can help you.

179
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:33,120
Miku!

180
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:37,560
Alright, fine, you win.

181
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:40,220
I'm human.

182
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:43,200
Or, I guess you could say I was.

183
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:47,300
I was a normal little girl who loves singing more than anything.

184
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:50,260
My name was Tsukino Yoimachi.

185
00:09:50,260 --> 00:10:01,240
My songs were all I had growing up, and when I was able to make a career out of singing and reach so many people with my music, I was as happy as I'd ever been.

186
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:05,100
Everyone loved my songs, which gave me great joy.

187
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:07,880
I was thrilled to share it with my fans.

188
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:14,240
But one day, after my first album dropped, my manager set me up with a producer.

189
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:17,700
He was from a TV station, so it seemed like a decent opportunity.

190
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:20,880
My manager told me to be extra nice.

191
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:25,040
Hold on, extra nice? Does that mean...

192
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:27,340
Yes, I'm afraid it means what you think.

193
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:29,640
I refused him, of course.

194
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,280
I didn't want to be a TV star anyway.

195
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:36,120
I just wanted to make music for myself and the people who loved it.

196
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:41,720
But then a scandal about the producer in me was published in a weekly magazine.

197
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:45,340
No one, not even my agency, was there to protect me.

198
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,180
You know what hurt me the most?

199
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,480
My fans.

200
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:55,520
No, the brutal reactions of the people I thought were my fans was the worst.

201
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:58,640
I tried to take comfort in my music.

202
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:02,400
As long as they listened to it, I thought they would come around.

203
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:03,640
But...

204
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:21,420
The stress became too much, and I lost my voice forever.

205
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:25,700
So you see, I stood up for myself, my pride.

206
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:29,620
And thanks to those evil men, my voice was gone.

207
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:32,500
I think what happened to you was a terrible thing.

208
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:36,280
The fact that your agents and your fans turned their backs on you makes me angry.

209
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:39,940
But even so, you can't blame the entire human race for that.

210
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:41,020
What do you know about it?

211
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,500
You men are all pigs!

212
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:46,120
Trust me, Miku, there are plenty of people out there who would love to listen to your music.

213
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:47,940
I bet you have droves of fans.

214
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:50,820
And I bet they don't care about some stupid made-up scandal.

215
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:52,900
No, you're wrong.

216
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:53,780
I'm not.

217
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:58,300
But you'll never find out, because you've made human beings your boogeyman, so you don't have to face your fears.

218
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:05,920
Shut up, shut up, shut up!

219
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,880
I'm sick of listening to your crap!

220
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:08,760
Idiot!

221
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:09,780
Moron!

222
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:10,980
Stupid head!

223
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:12,940
Miku, calm down.

224
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,440
You're just mad because you know I'm right.

225
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:15,620
Nope, wrong again.

226
00:12:15,620 --> 00:12:19,780
I'm mad because you're a complete jackass, you stupid, stupid man!

227
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,780
You're so annoying.

228
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:21,500
Damn it.

229
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:25,500
I can't leave Yoshino, Kaguya, or Yuzuru to you after all, can I?

230
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:28,440
I'm definitely sealing your spirit powers after this.

231
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:31,660
Are you trying to tell me to go back to how I was?

232
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:31,900
There we are!

233
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:32,200
Come on!

234
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:34,020
You're just a mute, hopeless, sat in a row?

235
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,680
No, I didn't say that!

236
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:42,920
Don't you get it?

237
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:47,980
I want you to conquer your fears and sing with your real voice instead of hiding behind this one and controlling people.

238
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:50,200
Stop talking like you know everything about me!

239
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:54,180
As long as I can use this voice to control people, I can be the best idol there is.

240
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:56,620
Without this power, who would choose to listen to me?

241
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,200
You don't get it, do you?

242
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,360
I'm nothing without this!

243
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,840
I would listen to you, Miku!

244
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:04,420
I did listen.

245
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:06,800
It was only one song.

246
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:10,360
But it was good, and you gave it your all.

247
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:11,780
I heard your passion.

248
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:12,860
You lie.

249
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:15,180
I don't believe you, Shido, not one bit.

250
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:19,700
When I was being dragged through the gutter and a single fan came to my defense, I was all alone.

251
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:22,140
My back was against the wall and no one came to help.

252
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:23,920
Well, I'm here now, Miku.

253
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:27,260
And I know there are tons of fans out there like me who will do the same.

254
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:33,900
Miku, if you're right when you say you have nothing without your power, just know at the very least you'll have me.

255
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:38,360
Well, thanks, but I know you'll break your promise.

256
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,300
I won't believe your lies!

257
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:41,260
You know what?

258
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,560
You need to learn to trust people.

259
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:43,160
Leave me alone!

260
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:45,800
If you would just give them a chance, you might find out that...

261
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,020
I can't hear you!

262
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,720
Stupid, stupid, stupid!

263
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:52,420
Well, I'm pretty sure this is it.

264
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:54,300
Hold on, Toka.

265
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:56,140
We'll have you back soon.

266
00:13:57,260 --> 00:14:02,540
Origami Tobiichi.

267
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,880
I must admit, I didn't expect to see you here today.

268
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:11,440
You're brave, but considering that mishmash of equipment you're carrying, you're also quite foolish.

269
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:14,580
It's equipment from a terrorist group we uncovered.

270
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,760
There's no ID restriction on it.

271
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,080
This is the only place that escaped HQ's retrieval order.

272
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,880
Please know that I say this out of concern.

273
00:14:23,180 --> 00:14:24,920
If I were you, I'd tread carefully.

274
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:26,940
Or you'll die today.

275
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:29,200
If I can save Shido, it'll be worth it.

276
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:31,120
So you do whatever you have to do!

277
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:41,660
If you think an attack like that is going to work, then you're more foolish than I thought.

278
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:43,740
